Rule 1 (dimension of the input array must be at least 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (integer split sections must be positive and divide the size of first dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ v_2 > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) % v_2 = 0
>>
Rule 3 (indices tensor must be 1D and have integer data type)
{v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 5
>>
Rule 4 (split indices in a tuple must be within the bounds of the split dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_2[i] ≤ shape(v_1, 0))
>>
Rule 5 (split indices in a list must be within the bounds of the split dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_2[i] ≤ shape(v_1, 0))
>>
Rule 8 (indices tensor must be 1D and elements within bounds of the split dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ min(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_2) ≤ shape(v_1, 0)
>>
Rule 9 (split indices in a list must be sorted in non-decreasing order)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 2] : v_2[i] ≤ v_2[i + 1])
>>
Rule 11 (split index tensor must be 1D and have integer data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5
>>
Rule 13 (split indices in a list must be sorted in non-decreasing order)
{v_1 : list(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 2] : v_1[i] ≤ v_1[i + 1]
>>
Rule 14 (split indices in a tuple must be sorted in non-decreasing order)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 2] : v_1[i] ≤ v_1[i + 1]
>>
Rule 15 (number of split sections in a list should not exceed the size of the split dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ v_2.len ≤ shape(v_1, 0)
